Z||000012||LZeitgeist||10-30-2001||09:57 AM||||Also, please remember Cliff's request about signatures... (bolding by me of Cliff's otherwise unaltered text)<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I've noticed that some signatures are a bit beyond what they are meant for. If you are using images in your signature, please keep in mind that not everybody has a broadband connection. Some threads load very slow simply because the browser needs to load a couple of hundred K's of signatures. <B>So try to keep them below 30K max.</B><P>Also, some signature images are way too large. <B>If your signature image is higher than 4 lines of text, chances are it's annoying the heck out of people.</B>Repetition - i.e. displaying your signature with every response in the same thread - is also not preferable.<P>If you want to include a link to your website in your signature, try doing this with a text link. I've seen animated banners in some people's signature. One of the nice things about this forum is that it has no banners. Please keep it this way. Most people find banners annoying and I'm already receiving complaints from members about the banners in signatures. <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I know you're not done with it yet, but that pic, while pretty cool, is *way* taller than 4 lines of text. So here's hoping future sig-related problems can be avoided...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jay||10-30-2001||11:41 AM||||I keep it big to work on.  Once they take it off the web, then they can resize the pic for their signature.  I don't want to piss Cliff off <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
